  "runtimeContract": [
    "Binary128 arguments are low/high i64 pairs. A binary128 or int128 result uses an initial i32 result pointer.",
    "Comparison results and 32-bit integer conversions are i32; 64-bit integer conversions are i64. SF/DF use f32/f64.",
    "Existing runtime supplies IEEE default round-to-nearest/ties-to-even; this scope does not add dynamic rounding modes or floating exception flags.",
    "libquadmath headers, GNU q-suffixed library calls, GNU q constant builtins and complex128 are outside this selected type/operator support scope unless independently implemented and qualified.",
    "Existing long-double math and text conversion APIs can be used with explicit long-double conversions; actual C/C++ fixtures must qualify those bridges."
  ],
